  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CATUS Youth Section</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is implemented in Serbia. The main outcome areas it contributes to are advancing equality and workers rights. The main rights holders are youth members of trade unions. Through seminars, mobilising and organising the project aims to achieve progressive development within the outcome areas.Project OrganisationsThis project is a cooperation between Confederation of Autonomous Trade Unions of Serbia (CATUS), Run folkhgskola and the Palme Center. CATUS Youth Section represents the Confederation&apos;s youth members, while Run is an educational organisation with a solid experience in training workers in Sweden.Project ObjectiveThe project objective is that 20 young people under the age of 35 become decision-makers within trade unions and voice the labour related needs of the entire youth movement in Serbia.Actor groups--Decision makers-- Government at all levels Socio Economic Councils --Actors in Cooperation-- NGOs ETUC, ITUC --Rights holders-- Youth members of trade union</narrative>
  </description>
